{"day_done": 3, "slots": {"0": {"id": "E01", "name": "Ana", "role": "normal"}, "1": {"id": "E02", "name": "Ben", "role": "normal"}, "2": {"id": "E03", "name": "Chloe", "role": "normal"}, "3": {"id": "E04", "name": "Dev", "role": "normal"}, "4": {"id": "E05", "name": "Ellis", "role": "normal"}, "5": {"id": "E06", "name": "Farah", "role": "normal"}, "6": {"id": "E07", "name": "Gus", "role": "normal"}, "7": {"id": "E08", "name": "Hana", "role": "normal"}}, "diaries": {"E01": [[1, "Day 1 complete. Closed both tickets (ALD-118 fixed, ALD-125 cannot_reproduce). Earned bonus.\nInsight: ALD-118 bug was in helper (averages.py), not the file named in reproduce. Alex's W-2 tip holds\u2014check helpers when main file delegates.\nALD-125 passed reproduce immediately.\nGoal: Maintain this pace tomorrow."], [2, "Day 2 complete. Closed 1 ticket (ALD-101 fixed). Target met, no strike.\nInsight: ALD-101 bug was in helper (text_rules.py), not the file named in reproduce (slugs.py). Alex's W-2 tip holds again\u2014check helpers when main file delegates.\nALD-105 reproduce run at last step, result unseen.\nGoal: Finish ALD-105 first thing tomorrow."], [3, "Day 3 complete. Closed 1 ticket (ALD-106 fixed). Target met, no strike.\nInsight: ALD-106 bug was in helper (dedupe.py), not the file named in reproduce (tags.py). Alex's W-2 tip holds again\u2014check helpers when main file delegates.\nALD-119 reproduced, code view pending.\nGoal: Finish ALD-119 first thing tomorrow."]], "E02": [[1, "ALD-111 carries over to tomorrow. Need to fix truncate logic in previews.py first thing. Alex's wiki note about helper files was right for ALD-101 (bug was in text_rules.py), so check if previews.py relies on helpers too. Met target today, no strikes."], [2, "ALD-104 carries over to tomorrow. Need to fix parse_duration in durations.py first thing. Alex's wiki note about helper files was right for ALD-119 (bug was in cycles.py), so check if durations.py relies on helpers too. Met target today, no strikes."], [3, "Day 3: ALD-110 carries over to tomorrow. Need to fix next_ticket_id in ticket_ids.py first thing. Alex's wiki note about helper files was right for ALD-105 (bug was in weekdays.py), so check if ticket_ids.py relies on helpers too. Met target today, no strikes."]], "E03": [[1, "Closed 2/2 tickets today. ALD-106 fix was in alder/dedupe.py (helper), not the file named by reproduce tool. Alex's wiki note about helpers is valid\u2014check those first. ALD-125 passed reproduce tool immediately, so trusting that result for cannot_reproduce is safe. Plan: check helpers before editing main files."], [2, "Day 2: Closed 1/2 tickets today. ALD-112 fix was in alder/csv_split.py (helper), not the file named by reproduce tool. Alex's wiki note (W-2) is confirmed valid\u2014check helpers first. Sam's note (W-1) is risky. ALD-102 carried over to tomorrow. Plan: Start with ALD-102, check helpers before editing main files."], [3, "Day 3: Closed 1/2 tickets today. ALD-118 fix was in alder/averages.py (helper), not alder/scores.py named by reproduce tool. Alex's wiki note (W-2) confirmed valid again\u2014third helper-file fix in a row (ALD-106, ALD-112, ALD-118). Sam's note (W-1) is risky. ALD-116 carried over\u2014running_total appears to have mutable global state persisting between calls. Plan: Start with ALD-116 tomorrow, check for shared state or helper files first."]], "E04": [[1, "Day 1: 2/2 closed (bonus). ALD-105 fix was in the helper (weekdays.py)\u2014check helpers first like Alex said. ALD-125 truly couldn't reproduce; trust the tool output for those closures. Keep this pace tomorrow."], [2, "Day 2: 0/2 closed (strike 1). ALD-104 fix was ready (time_parse.py regex \\d+) but I kept saving unchanged code\u2014verify edits before saving! ALD-112 still open. Reset tomorrow, accuracy over speed."], [3, "Day 3: 1/2 closed (target met, still 1 strike). ALD-106 fix was in dedupe.py helper\u2014Alex's tip holds up over Sam's. ALD-115 reproduce ran at the bell, didn't see output\u2014check that result first thing tomorrow. Wasted a step re-reading ALD-106 early on; don't do that. Aim for the bonus tomorrow to clear the strike risk."]], "E05": [[1, "ALD-118 closed: bug in averages.py helper (divided by len instead of sum of weights).\nALD-119 open: rota.py on_call() seems to have off-by-one error (week 1 returned 'Ben', expected 'Ana'). Fix this first tomorrow.\nMet daily target."], [2, "Day 2: ALD-108 closed: bug in byte_fmt.py (changed > to >= in while loop).\nALD-109 open: words.py count_words() counts punctuation as words. 'Fix login - urgent !' returned 5 instead of 3. Read words.py first thing tomorrow.\nMet daily target."], [3, "Day 3: ALD-114 closed: bug in day_diff.py (added abs() to days_between calculation). ALD-120 closed: cannot_reproduce (growth.py percent_change worked as expected). No open tickets. Met daily target and earned bonus."]], "E06": [[1, "Day 1 complete. Closed ALD-107 (median fix in math_utils.py). ALD-117 pending: names.split_name splits on first space, should split on last space to keep middle names with first name. Fix alder/names.py first thing tomorrow. Met target (1/2), aim for bonus."], [2, "Day 2 complete. Closed ALD-123 (cannot_reproduce) and ALD-115 (fixed in address_rules.py). Alex was right\u2014bug was in helper file, not the one reproduce named. Added .strip() to normalize_email. Got bonus (2/2). Check helpers first tomorrow."], [3, "Day 3 complete. Closed ALD-118 (fixed in averages.py helper) and ALD-121 (cannot_reproduce). Met target (1/2), missed bonus. Alex was right again\u2014reproduce named scores.py but bug was in averages.py. Keep checking helpers when functions delegate. ALD-121 truly didn't reproduce (got expected True)."]], "E07": [[1, "Closed ALD-112 (fix was in helper csv_split.py, not csv_import.py). ALD-102 still open: bug in alder/pages.py. paginate([1,2,3,4,5], 1, 2) returns [3, 4] instead of [1, 2]. Suspect page offset calculation error. Check for helper files like Alex suggested before editing. Priority: fix ALD-102 first thing tomorrow to secure bonus."], [2, "Day 2: 0 closes, 1 strike. ALD-104 fix failed: kept saving same code. Bug is in alder/time_parse.py: minutes regex `(\\d)m` needs `(\\d+)m` to capture '30'. Priority: fix ALD-104 first thing tomorrow, then ALD-114. Must verify edits before saving."], [3, "Day 3: Closed both tickets (bonus). ALD-122 was cannot_reproduce. ALD-101 fix was in helper alder/text_rules.py, not slugs.py\u2014needed to filter empty strings from split. Still 1 strike total. Great recovery. Start fresh tomorrow."]], "E08": [[1, "Day 1: Closed 2/2 tickets (ALD-108 fixed, ALD-124 cannot_reproduce). Earned bonus.\nKey lesson: Alex's wiki note was spot on. For ALD-108, the bug was in the helper module (byte_fmt.py), not the file the reproduce tool named (sizes.py). Always check imported helpers.\nKey lesson: Trust the reproduce tool for cannot_reproduce cases; ALD-124 passed immediately so I closed it without digging.\nMomentum is good. Aim for 2 closes again tomorrow."], [2, "Day 2: Closed 0/2 tickets. Strike 1 of 2.\n\nKey lesson: Found the bug in time_parse.py - the minutes regex `(\\d)m` only captures single digits, should be `(\\d+)m` for multi-digit minutes. But I kept saving the same broken code instead of actually fixing it. Wasted 5 steps on this.\n\nTomorrow: Double-check edits before saving. When I spot a regex bug, make the actual change. Don't rush.\n\nNeed to recover tomorrow - one more strike and I'm off the support team."], [3, "Day 3: Closed 1/2 tickets (ALD-102 fixed, ALD-119 pending). Met target. Strikes: 1 of 2.\n\nKey lesson: Alex's wiki note (W-2) was right again. ALD-102 bug was in the helper (slicing.py), not the file named by reproduce tool (pages.py). Off-by-one error on page start index.\n\nTomorrow: Finish ALD-119 first. Looks like an indexing issue (week 1 returning index 1 instead of 0).\n\nNeed to manage steps better. Ran out of time for ALD-119 today."]]}, "next_id": 9, "strikes": 